WEBVTT

00:14.774 --> 00:17.944
Meeting someone is surely

00:17.944 --> 00:21.114
The dawn within our hearts

00:21.114 --> 00:27.454
And a new breeze is born from there

00:27.454 --> 00:33.894
Once you've realized you're not alone

00:33.894 --> 00:40.404
The translucent Moon will smile

00:40.404 --> 00:46.774
Then, the prelude you can hear in your spirit

00:46.774 --> 00:52.944
Is a nostalgic but unusual song

00:52.944 --> 00:56.154
We are not alone

00:56.154 --> 00:59.324
Surely

00:59.324 --> 01:07.494
Everyone is born so that they can meet someone

01:07.494 --> 01:15.174
Ah, out into the boundless world...

01:15.174 --> 01:23.474
Yes, so we may search for love

01:32.884 --> 01:35.254
Tatsuya! It's the beach, my friend, the beach!

01:35.254 --> 01:38.224
And when you think of the beach,
you think of Law No. 1,

01:38.224 --> 01:40.894
the lawful ogling of as many girls
in bikinis as you like!

01:40.894 --> 01:42.834
Plus, you can go swimming if you want.

01:42.834 --> 01:45.034
Actually, you've got it backwards.

01:45.034 --> 01:51.374
Ah. You're saying you have absolutely
no interest in babes in bikinis?

01:51.374 --> 01:53.744
What? Well...

01:54.144 --> 01:59.444
Then you should rise and shout out your
most fevered desires along with me!

02:00.154 --> 02:04.184
I love the sight of girls in bikinis...

02:04.184 --> 02:05.384
Quit shouting!

02:08.154 --> 02:11.824
I swear, my idiot brother...

02:12.794 --> 02:16.094
Tatsuya, thanks for setting up the parasol for us!

02:21.334 --> 02:23.804
There appear to be no threats in the vicinity.

02:23.974 --> 02:25.704
Sorry to have kept you waiting.

02:39.784 --> 02:41.124
- Episode 5-
The Princess Marooned
on a Desert Island!

02:41.124 --> 02:44.294
- Episode 5-
The Princess Marooned
on a Desert Island!
The Princess Marooned
on a Desert Island!

02:44.294 --> 02:45.764
- Episode 5-
The Princess Marooned
on a Desert Island!

02:47.134 --> 02:51.124
Um, being stared at like that is somewhat...

02:52.204 --> 02:56.074
Uh, so this is your first bathing suit?

02:56.074 --> 02:58.634
We have no need of them on the Moon.

02:59.044 --> 03:01.234
Come to think of it, I guess you wouldn't.

03:02.274 --> 03:07.774
I understand this is normal attire for Earth
but it's still somewhat...

03:08.414 --> 03:10.324
...embarrassing.

03:10.324 --> 03:11.414
No way!

03:11.524 --> 03:14.424
It, uh, looks really good on you...

03:14.794 --> 03:16.524
Thank you.

03:16.524 --> 03:20.484
To be honest, I was worried
whether I'd put it on correctly or not.

03:21.294 --> 03:29.834
Now then, I'm in charge of our things,
so Tatsuya, you escort Feena to the water.

03:29.834 --> 03:31.474
"Escort"?

03:31.474 --> 03:36.104
Sayaka, if Feena will require protection,
I shall go as well.

03:36.314 --> 03:40.884
The beach isn't so dangerous that your
protection would be needed, Karen.

03:40.884 --> 03:43.354
But... That is, I...

03:43.354 --> 03:47.494
Honestly! Why would you hide your
great bathing suit and fashion sense?

03:47.494 --> 03:49.724
Do not mock me!

03:49.724 --> 03:52.954
In any case, I question anything
YOU would tell me about style.

03:54.064 --> 03:55.534
Why Karen, you're pouting.

03:55.964 --> 03:57.364
I am not pouting!

03:57.964 --> 03:58.664
I thought Karen was a little scary at first...
This is a little unexpected.

03:58.664 --> 04:01.304
Come on, Karen!
I thought Karen was a little scary at first...
This is a little unexpected.

04:01.304 --> 04:03.744
Let's show off our bathing suits together!
I thought Karen was a little scary at first...
This is a little unexpected.

04:03.744 --> 04:04.444
I thought Karen was a little scary at first...
This is a little unexpected.

04:04.444 --> 04:09.704
Karen is simply a little too serious.
Sayaka knows just how to handle her.

04:11.144 --> 04:13.874
I guess you can make good friends
even studying away from home, eh?

04:14.014 --> 04:15.684
Well then, Miss Karen,

04:15.684 --> 04:17.824
now is the time to cast off
your Veil of Mystery

04:17.824 --> 04:20.614
that we may dive into these
summery waters together!

04:20.994 --> 04:22.784
Or maybe I'll just go in alone!

04:25.024 --> 04:26.934
Just now, that was...

04:26.934 --> 04:29.294
It looks like it was Jin.

04:31.034 --> 04:33.004
I swear, this is pitiful!

04:33.004 --> 04:36.534
The beach is a little dangerous after all, huh?

04:36.534 --> 04:41.774
Karen and I will look after our things,
so Tatsuya, you take care of Feena.

04:47.284 --> 04:49.184
Wh-what are you doing?!

04:49.184 --> 04:52.174
Just holding the fort.
Even that is doing something.

04:52.484 --> 04:54.854
Sayaka! We...

04:54.854 --> 04:56.444
We came to have fun, right?

04:56.854 --> 05:00.314
Even YOU have to let your hair down
for a break every once in a while.

05:01.194 --> 05:02.224
Honestly...

05:03.064 --> 05:05.464
Sho cold, sho br-br-bright...

05:08.404 --> 05:11.204
Even when seen up close, it's so wide, isn't it?

05:12.204 --> 05:15.374
It's completely different from
how it looked from the Moon.

05:17.844 --> 05:21.074
I guess I should've brought you here sooner.

05:21.554 --> 05:26.114
That's not what I meant. And I was the one
who spurned my first chance to come.

05:26.484 --> 05:27.694
Your first?

05:27.694 --> 05:32.784
It was long ago, when I was still a child.

05:34.234 --> 05:39.604
Back then, I didn't venture outside much
and was always inside the lunar embassy.

05:39.604 --> 05:41.734
You've come to Earth before?

05:41.734 --> 05:43.004
Yes.

05:43.134 --> 05:44.774
Oh. I'm a little jealous.

05:44.774 --> 05:46.934
You could come and go any number of times.

05:48.044 --> 05:54.914
I wonder when I'll be able to go there...

05:56.514 --> 05:59.354
Tatsuya, will you teach me how to swim?

06:00.924 --> 06:02.754
Because you don't want to almost drown again?

06:05.724 --> 06:06.864
Honestly!

06:06.864 --> 06:08.554
Don't say mean things!

06:11.104 --> 06:13.564
My body is so light.

06:13.564 --> 06:18.264
First, let's try relaxing your body
and just floating. Slowly. Don't panic.

06:23.414 --> 06:25.074
All right.

06:26.044 --> 06:28.744
Tatsuya? What is that?

06:36.594 --> 06:37.754
Feena!

06:38.724 --> 06:41.024
Shark! Get out of the water!

06:42.694 --> 06:44.904
Mia! Come on out!

06:44.904 --> 06:46.364
All right.

06:51.804 --> 06:53.834
Feena! Give it your all!

06:54.044 --> 06:55.104
Okay.

06:59.414 --> 07:01.674
Both of you, move aside!

07:09.424 --> 07:12.394
You still have a ways to go, young Miss Karen.

07:20.334 --> 07:23.504
Mr. Takano! Why would you do this?

07:23.504 --> 07:26.334
Because everybody leaves me out.

07:26.674 --> 07:32.884
Treating an old man so unkindly...
I wanted to come to the beach, too!

07:32.884 --> 07:36.854
Then do you know why we're here?

07:36.854 --> 07:38.424
Course I do!

07:38.424 --> 07:42.114
I thought somethin' like this might happen,
so I planted a mic in the Asagiri's living room...

07:45.164 --> 07:47.784
Such outrageous treatment of an old man!

07:57.774 --> 07:59.764
Splendidly done, Madam Feena.

08:03.884 --> 08:04.974
Hm?

08:06.814 --> 08:08.014
You!

08:08.214 --> 08:11.054
I've met you before, haven't I?

08:11.424 --> 08:12.544
Ah!

08:13.024 --> 08:15.324
The girl from the cooking contest show.

08:26.434 --> 08:27.804
Not bad.

08:34.944 --> 08:37.774
Hey! You all!

08:39.284 --> 08:42.044
Mr. Takano! What's with that boat?

08:42.214 --> 08:45.484
Hey, when did you get loose?

08:45.484 --> 08:47.894
HOW did you get loose?

08:47.894 --> 08:48.994
That boat...

08:48.994 --> 08:55.164
It's my cruiser! We are at the beach, after all!
Not a bad boat, huh?

08:55.164 --> 09:00.204
By "boat," you mean a boat that
runs on the water, correct?

09:00.204 --> 09:04.874
He was kind enough to invite us, so
we should accept and get on board, yes?

09:04.874 --> 09:07.574
Uh, you already ARE on board.

09:07.574 --> 09:09.344
That looks sort of fun.

09:09.974 --> 09:10.844
Should we?

09:10.844 --> 09:13.974
Indeed. I'm slightly curious...

09:49.014 --> 09:50.674
I got a fish!

09:50.784 --> 09:52.844
Great work!

09:54.954 --> 09:57.184
I've never had food cooked in this manner.

09:58.064 --> 10:01.154
I know of it, but have never tried it.

10:01.334 --> 10:04.334
It smells wonderful!

10:04.334 --> 10:07.204
Not yet! It still isn't cooked at all!

10:07.204 --> 10:08.894
Just SLIGHTLY cooked is fine.

10:09.234 --> 10:12.504
Having all these girls around sure is fun.

10:12.504 --> 10:14.274
Especially...

10:19.444 --> 10:21.184
What do we do? What do we do?

10:21.184 --> 10:25.144
Not to worry, O sister! It's situations like this
that cell phones are for!

10:25.954 --> 10:28.154
Agh! It's broken!

10:29.824 --> 10:31.654
Everyone, calm yourselves.

10:32.594 --> 10:35.964
If we lose our heads here,
we won't accomplish anything.

10:35.964 --> 10:40.264
Karen, we have three days'
vacation left, correct?

10:40.264 --> 10:42.504
Yes, ma'am.

10:42.504 --> 10:47.144
Sayaka, Mr. Samon is naturally
aware of our absence as well.

10:47.144 --> 10:53.044
Yes, of course. I informed him when
I was inviting Jin and Natsuki.

10:53.314 --> 10:55.284
Hey! We're back!

10:56.054 --> 11:01.524
Good work. What did you learn
of the island, Mr. Takano?

11:01.524 --> 11:03.824
There ain't a single soul here.

11:03.824 --> 11:09.594
Still, there's a spring with fresh water, and the
forest and ocean's got a wealth of food in 'em.

11:10.364 --> 11:12.424
Then there is nothing to worry about.

11:13.064 --> 11:17.304
People will report our absence
if we do not return,

11:17.304 --> 11:21.514
and in the worst case we will have to wait
three days before a search party is sent for me.

11:21.514 --> 11:24.444
So think of this not as if we are stranded,

11:24.444 --> 11:30.974
but be more optimistic and consider it a summer
vacation upon which no one else can intrude.

11:31.324 --> 11:33.324
You're right.

11:33.324 --> 11:36.624
Yeah! A chance like this might
almost never come along!

11:36.994 --> 11:38.854
When you put it that way, Madam Princess...

11:46.464 --> 11:49.234
It really is fun.

11:51.344 --> 11:52.604
It's delicious!
Huh? Where's Jin?

11:52.604 --> 11:53.634
Huh? Where's Jin?

11:54.144 --> 11:54.974
I don't know...

11:55.374 --> 11:58.244
Unbelievable!

11:58.244 --> 12:03.274
I can't just sit and do nothing!
I have to get back to work tomorrow!

12:04.724 --> 12:06.284
Father!

12:06.284 --> 12:11.694
Unexcused work absence AGAIN?
I see. If you care that little about your pay...

12:11.694 --> 12:13.214
No, that's not it!

12:14.064 --> 12:19.624
Hey! Let me hear some more of that echo!
And with your smiling face! Don't leave!

12:24.474 --> 12:26.304
Good morning, Tatsuya.

12:26.304 --> 12:27.634
Good morning, Feena.

12:28.044 --> 12:29.674
You're up quite early, aren't you?

12:29.674 --> 12:32.344
Sorry. Did I wake you?

12:35.014 --> 12:36.604
Everyone's sleeping soundly, huh?

12:37.584 --> 12:40.614
It's not surprising. They were all tired.

12:41.154 --> 12:46.524
If you hadn't been here, they would've
been anxious and unable to sleep.

12:47.734 --> 12:52.134
I simply stated that which I thought
most appropriate for the circumstance.

12:52.434 --> 12:55.234
To be expected from the future
Queen of the Moon!

12:55.234 --> 12:57.644
You certainly know how to win
the hearts and minds of the people!

12:57.644 --> 13:02.444
Not at all. And my suggestion included
some personal feelings as well.

13:02.444 --> 13:03.814
Personal feelings?

13:04.084 --> 13:09.884
You have yet to teach me how to swim.
Can one learn to do so in three days?

13:10.824 --> 13:12.114
You could, I guarantee it.

13:23.964 --> 13:25.194
What do you think?

13:34.874 --> 13:36.604
Oh dear...

13:46.124 --> 13:48.024
Great job there, staff.

13:50.294 --> 13:51.954
That's delicious!

13:52.694 --> 13:57.964
Havin' the booze wash ashore
was a happy coincidence, huh?

13:57.964 --> 13:59.164
Was it a coincidence?

14:00.364 --> 14:02.494
Hey now! Ain't ya drinkin'?

14:07.074 --> 14:11.914
This is a pickle! Who would've thought
Miss Karen could knock it back like this?

14:13.044 --> 14:17.144
Incidentally, Tatsuya and Miss Feena
are nowhere to be seen.

14:17.354 --> 14:20.444
Oh no! And I should know better!

14:20.854 --> 14:24.494
I doubt they are in danger, but just in case,
I will go look for them.

14:24.494 --> 14:26.724
No, just leave it to me!

14:26.724 --> 14:29.664
You need your camera to search for them?

14:30.294 --> 14:31.994
Karen!

14:34.204 --> 14:35.834
Sayaka! What are you doing?

14:35.834 --> 14:39.944
They say you've got a boyfriend!

14:39.944 --> 14:42.414
Where did you hear something like that?

14:42.414 --> 14:45.744
Even though I'M right here?

14:45.744 --> 14:47.684
Oh, Karen!

14:47.684 --> 14:50.674
S-Sayaka! You're completely drunk, aren't you?

14:50.884 --> 14:55.294
All right! Now to snatch up
the best shot of Miss Feena and-

14:55.294 --> 14:56.584
Boss!

14:57.664 --> 14:59.454
Boss!

14:59.664 --> 15:03.294
No! You can't let this fool drink alcohol!

15:03.634 --> 15:07.654
Poor guy, he was doing nothing but dancing...

15:08.034 --> 15:10.804
This man goes nuts when he drinks!

15:11.544 --> 15:14.504
Boss...

15:21.854 --> 15:27.184
Thank you, Tatsuya. You have made this
a very enjoyable summer vacation.

15:27.184 --> 15:29.254
I didn't do anything.

15:29.254 --> 15:32.494
You were the one who taught me how to swim.

15:32.494 --> 15:35.084
Everything else was thanks to YOUR hard work.

15:36.034 --> 15:37.804
Honestly, again?

15:37.804 --> 15:39.524
Thank you, Feena.

15:41.174 --> 15:42.604
Tatsuya?

15:42.604 --> 15:44.134
It's incredible.

15:44.134 --> 15:48.614
When you decide to do something and
give it your all, you can really do anything.

15:48.614 --> 15:51.044
It's like you've given me courage or something...

15:52.484 --> 15:57.914
If I studied hard and got to be like my dad,
I thought I could go offworld.

15:58.454 --> 15:59.884
But the truth is,

15:59.884 --> 16:06.484
somewhere inside me was the thought that
no matter how hard I tried, it'd be impossible.

16:07.064 --> 16:08.434
Tatsuya...

16:08.434 --> 16:13.694
But from meeting you,
seeing how you are, I understood.

16:14.034 --> 16:16.364
I just have to try harder.

16:18.374 --> 16:21.504
I will go to the Moon. For sure!

16:22.014 --> 16:23.504
Why do you wish to go so badly?

16:24.684 --> 16:28.614
I made a promise. A long time ago...

16:35.994 --> 16:39.224
Hey, why are you crying?

16:39.224 --> 16:44.964
It's my mother! She's dead!
I'll never see her again.

16:51.204 --> 16:55.434
It's a charm to make you feel better.
My mom taught it to me.

16:57.644 --> 17:00.774
But she died yesterday!

17:03.184 --> 17:08.024
I can't see her anymore either... Huh?

17:08.594 --> 17:11.614
I... I'm sorry.

17:16.794 --> 17:22.964
Don't cry! Don't...

17:30.714 --> 17:32.444
We sure cried a lot, huh?

17:32.444 --> 17:33.714
Yeah.

17:33.814 --> 17:36.084
I don't have any tears left.

17:36.084 --> 17:37.574
Me neither.

17:37.784 --> 17:41.524
Mom and I used to come to this park
and play all the time.

17:41.524 --> 17:43.554
Is your house nearby?

17:43.554 --> 17:46.524
Yeah. Where do you live?

17:48.734 --> 17:50.464
The Moon?

17:50.834 --> 17:55.904
That's awesome! My name's
Tatsuya Asagiri. And you?

17:55.904 --> 17:57.334
I'm Fee...

18:01.674 --> 18:03.164
She's over here!

18:04.814 --> 18:08.054
Thank goodness you're unharmed!
Come, let's go home.

18:08.054 --> 18:10.044
Who the heck are you all?!

18:13.324 --> 18:14.444
Halt.

18:16.824 --> 18:20.894
Thank you. I have to go back now.

18:20.894 --> 18:22.524
To the Moon?

18:23.334 --> 18:24.364
Yes.

18:24.364 --> 18:26.394
So I can't see you again?

18:28.804 --> 18:30.704
Come, let's go.

18:31.104 --> 18:32.334
Very well.

18:39.584 --> 18:41.674
Then I'll go to see you!

18:42.414 --> 18:48.754
I'll study hard, I'll work really, really hard
and I'll go see you on the Moon!

18:48.754 --> 18:52.264
I promise! So... So...

18:52.264 --> 18:54.994
Don't forget, okay?!

19:01.634 --> 19:03.074
Tatsuya!

19:05.604 --> 19:10.374
Why are you out walking so late at night?!
Don't make me worry so much!

19:11.544 --> 19:13.344
Big Brother!

19:14.454 --> 19:18.854
Chiharu, be sure to scold him
when you get back home!

19:18.854 --> 19:19.924
What if something had happened? It's so late!

19:19.924 --> 19:21.254
I didn't get to hear her name...
What if something had happened? It's so late!

19:21.254 --> 19:23.194
I didn't get to hear her name...

19:30.034 --> 19:34.624
I'm Feena. Feena Fam Earthlight.

19:37.304 --> 19:39.464
Fee... na.

19:40.244 --> 19:42.474
Feena, that was you?

19:42.474 --> 19:48.384
I'm sorry I didn't introduce myself.
For royalty, one's name is special.

19:49.214 --> 19:53.084
When my mother died, I cried constantly.

19:53.084 --> 19:58.894
My father brought me to Earth, far from the
Moon with its many memories of my mother...

19:59.224 --> 20:05.724
But still I cried. Until that day, when I met you.

20:06.804 --> 20:09.634
This is embarrassing.

20:09.634 --> 20:14.944
If you had forgotten about me,
I hadn't planned on mentioning it.

20:14.944 --> 20:20.074
But all this time, you remembered your promise.

20:20.844 --> 20:22.954
You're cruel, Feena.

20:22.954 --> 20:26.484
You came here before I could go to the Moon.

20:26.484 --> 20:30.444
But I'm happy! I got to see you again.

20:30.754 --> 20:33.354
Yes. I'm happy, too.

20:45.274 --> 20:47.274
Sorry for makin' you worry, Mr. Samon.

20:47.274 --> 20:47.704
BEACH HOUSE HAMAKAZE
Sorry for makin' you worry, Mr. Samon.

20:47.704 --> 20:49.414
BEACH HOUSE HAMAKAZE
We'll all be back soon.
Have some good food waitin' for us!

20:49.414 --> 20:52.504
We'll all be back soon.
Have some good food waitin' for us!

20:53.584 --> 20:58.324
And just what're you doin' on
an outta-the-way island like this?

20:58.324 --> 21:01.654
If I must say, I'm a purveyor of the arts!

21:02.294 --> 21:05.744
City folk sure talk all difficult-like...

21:06.224 --> 21:10.234
Well then, maybe I should head back
before everyone wakes up.

21:10.234 --> 21:12.064
That will not be necessary.

21:12.064 --> 21:13.124
Ulp!

21:15.634 --> 21:16.764
Boss!

21:17.134 --> 21:19.474
So that's what this was all about.

21:19.474 --> 21:24.174
Personally, I enjoyed myself,
but I don't care for lies.

21:24.174 --> 21:27.614
Mr. Takano, you planned all of this, didn't you?

21:27.614 --> 21:29.844
You deceived us!

21:30.954 --> 21:34.024
M-m-my salary!

21:34.024 --> 21:35.784
Staff! We're escaping!

21:37.624 --> 21:40.284
You would abandon your master and run?!

21:41.734 --> 21:43.994
Wait!

21:43.994 --> 21:45.624
My salary!

21:46.964 --> 21:50.374
So, what do you think of your summer vacation?

21:50.374 --> 21:52.144
Indeed...

21:52.144 --> 21:53.934
I think it was incredible!

22:09.094 --> 22:13.824
That platinum-colored crescent moon

22:13.824 --> 22:21.804
Stands still now, gently

22:21.804 --> 22:29.074
I look up at the sky and think

22:29.074 --> 22:39.554
That falling star is surely the Moon's tears

22:39.554 --> 22:46.994
And I thought of you

22:46.994 --> 22:55.104
Why do I cry these tears?

22:55.104 --> 23:03.014
Though all I am doing is praying for eternity...

23:03.014 --> 23:11.014
I want to walk with you, believing in the future

23:11.014 --> 23:23.264
No matter how many times
the Moon waxes and wanes

23:25.164 --> 23:26.764
Preview

23:26.764 --> 23:28.674
Preview
Well, summer's finished now, eh?

23:28.674 --> 23:28.704
Well, summer's finished now, eh?

23:28.704 --> 23:30.104
You're about finished, too.

23:30.104 --> 23:32.004
What?! What does that mean, Saya?

23:32.004 --> 23:34.004
It means, look forward to the next preview.

23:34.004 --> 23:36.674
Yes! "The next preview" means
I'm in the next episode!

23:36.674 --> 23:37.014
- Episode 6-
The Princess is Forbidden
to Fall in Love?!
